# Code owners.
#
# The first version of this file assigned org teams (@platform-team, @catalog-team,
# @architecture, …). This is a personal repository, not an organization, so none of those
# handles could ever resolve: the file read like an access control and functioned as a
# comment. Fixed in #3.
#
# CODEOWNERS only *enforces* anything when a branch protection rule requires review from
# code owners; otherwise it is a routing hint. The protection rule on main is the real gate.
#
# The area boundaries below were right — only the handles were wrong. When this project
# gains an organization and teams, restore the per-team split rather than reinventing it.

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                        @morisempai

# Cross-cutting sources of truth. Root rules: services may NOT edit contracts/, shared/,
# .github/, or other services without a linked contract-change / shared-change issue.
#
# contracts/ is the source of truth for every service boundary (hard rule #2) — a change
# here can break every consumer at once.
/contracts/              @morisempai

# shared/ ships to every service simultaneously.
/shared/                 @morisempai

# CI/CD and repo governance. Changes here alter the checks applied to every other change,
# which makes this the most sensitive path in the repo.
/.github/                @morisempai

# Agent instructions and skills — these define how automated contributors behave.
/.claude/                @morisempai
/CLAUDE.md               @morisempai

# Infrastructure — blast radius beyond any single service.
/infra/                  @morisempai

# Architecture decisions.
/docs/adr/               @morisempai

# Services — each owned by its team when teams exist.
/services/gateway/       @morisempai
/services/catalog/       @morisempai
/services/availability/  @morisempai
/services/booking/       @morisempai
/services/payment/       @morisempai
/services/notification/  @morisempai
